    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, i get that it's a shock, but it's more than that. it feels like i've finished the game. there's no more levels to unlock, no more achievements to chase. i look at my life and i just don't see a reason to keep grinding. the drive is just... gone. what am i even supposed to do with the rest of my time if the point of it all was just getting here?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of having \"finished the game\" is often called the \"endgame blues,\" a profound midlife recalibration where the old goals no longer satisfy you. Many adults experience this specifically around their late 20s or 30s, feeling a collective sigh that there is nothing left to achieve but instead a new need to create. If the current drive feels empty, it might be beneficial to shift your primary mission from *achieving* to *becoming*, perhaps by adopting a hobby that isn't driven by success but simply by the joy of doing it.",
      "source": "target",
